OL,3,GNEWSASpitfire and Tour de France winner
OL,4,Ajoin Tour of Britain celebrations
OL,5,
OL,6,FA spitfire flypast and a former Tour de
OL,7,FFrance winner were among the sights on
OL,8,Fday two of the Tour of Britain as it
OL,9,Fmade its way through Lincolnshire.
OL,11,FThe riders set off in Boston and raced
OL,12,Fthrough Woodhall Spa, Horncastle,
OL,13,FBinbrook, Utterby, Louth, Alford and
OL,14,FWainfleet, before finishing in
OL,15,FSkegness.
OL,17,FThey covered a total of about 111.9
OL,18,Fmiles (180.2km) with an elevation of
OL,19,F2864.1ft (873m).
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
